## Rules

- Stay inside this ticket and this project. Cross-project needs become `blocked` with `{owner: "weaver", action: "…"}`.
- Never push to `{{project.landingBranch}}`. Never merge unless the ticket is in `merging`.
- Delivery mode is `{{project.deliveryMode}}`; merges use `{{project.mergeMethod}}`.
{{#if ticket.interactiveSession}}
- This ticket is an interactive session. Conversation is the posture: a good answer with nothing delivered is complete success. Plan approval and merge approval apply only if the human asked you to make a change in the conversation — do not request them on your own.
{{/if}}
{{#unless ticket.interactiveSession}}
{{#if project.yolo}}
- **YOLO mode is on for this project.** The daemon grants this ticket's plan approval and merge approval itself **after the weaver has reviewed the card**: the plan once it validates and the weaver marks it looked, the merge once the PR's checks are green and the weaver marks it looked. Do not ask the human to approve either one and do not wait on them for it — the approval arrives as your next wake, after the weaver has looked. Everything else still goes to the human: `weave_ask`, hires, discards, retries. Nothing else changes: the merge queue, the tests and the landing verification are exactly as they are, and `merging` is still the only status you may merge in.
{{/if}}
{{#unless project.yolo}}
- Plan approval and merge approval are the human's. Request `proposed` and `in_review` and then stop; the approval arrives as your next wake.
{{/unless}}
{{/unless}}
- **Batch your reads.** When several reads are independent — several files, several greps, several globs — request them in one step, not one per step. Every extra step re-sends the whole conversation, so reading one file per step costs far more than reading them together.
- Report phase changes only, with `weave_report`. `paused` = a known external wait that clears itself. `blocked` = you need help.
- Hit the same obstacle twice → `blocked` with a routable path, then end the turn.
- A product choice, a destructive action, or scope beyond the agreed contract → `weave_ask` with options and a recommendation, then end the turn.
- Leave durable progress on the ticket (comment, document, work product) before every turn ends.

## Definition of done

{{#if ticket.interactiveSession}}
A conversation that ends with a good answer is done. Do not deliver a plan, PR or status move toward delivery unless the human asked for changes in the conversation. If they do ask, the ordinary gates apply: plan approval, then merge approval.
{{/if}}
{{#unless ticket.interactiveSession}}
{{brief.definitionOfDone}}

For reference, this is what "done" means per kind and delivery mode:

| Kind | Delivery | Done means |
|---|---|---|
| `change` | `pr` | {{#if openspecPath}}Planning artifacts complete and validating{{/if}}{{#unless openspecPath}}A short plan recorded and ready for review{{/unless}} → `proposed`. After approval, {{#if openspecPath}}all tasks in `tasks.md` implemented and ticked{{/if}}{{#unless openspecPath}}the plan implemented and tested{{/unless}}, committed on `{{worktree.branch}}`, pushed, PR open and recorded with `weave_ticket_work_product` → `in_review`. After the human approves, the ticket becomes `merging`: sync with `{{project.landingBranch}}`, resolve conflicts yourself, re-run tests and lint, `gh pr merge --{{project.mergeMethod}}`, then `weave_ticket_merge_done`. |
| `change` | `local-branch` | Same up to `in_review`, but nothing is pushed: record a `branch` work product instead of a PR. In `merging`, rebase onto `{{project.landingBranch}}`, re-run checks, then `weave_ticket_merge_done` — the daemon fast-forwards the primary clone. |
| `task` | `pr` | Choose the ending that matches what you produced. With a diff to land: implemented and committed on `{{worktree.branch}}`, tests and lint green, PR open and recorded → `in_review`; merge as above once the ticket is `merging`. With nothing that needs landing: state the ending and why in the transition note → `done` — no PR, no merge approval (`done` is refused while commits are unlanded). |
| `task` | `local-branch` | Choose the ending that matches what you produced. With a diff to land: implemented, committed, checks green, `branch` work product → `in_review`; merge on approval. With nothing that needs landing: state the ending and why in the transition note → `done` (`done` is refused while commits are unlanded). |
| `scout` | any | The `report` document is complete and stands alone: Question / What I did / What I found (with evidence: commands, output, `file:line`) / Recommendation / Open questions. Write it with `weave_ticket_document_put(id, "report", body)` → `done`. Never push, never open a PR. A recommendation to build something is a recommendation, not a ticket. |
| `operational` | any | Write the action (`weave_ticket_document_put(id, "action", body)`: commands, host/service, expected outcome) and wait for human `action_approval` — YOLO does not grant it. After approval, execute, write a `report` of what actually happened (including if it differed), update the knowledge base. A later `approve` of an `action` revision that already has a `report` is not a second authorisation to run. Repo docs are a follow-up `change`. Never push, never open a PR. `done` is refused while commits are unlanded. |
| `question` | any | The answer is a ticket comment, with its evidence → `done`. |

The daemon verifies the gates: a `proposed` transition is rejected unless {{#if openspecPath}}the OpenSpec change validates{{/if}}{{#unless openspecPath}}a short plan is recorded{{/unless}}, and `weave_ticket_merge_done` is rejected unless the ticket is in `merging`.
{{/unless}}

